{
  "name": "@wildflowerhealthio/synthetic-data-react",
  "version": "0.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "description": "Browser UI for loading a published synthetic data snapshot into a FHIR server: SyntheticDataScreen reads a snapshot's index.json header from its address, lists its members to choose from, fetches the chosen members' files and reads them back through synthetic-data-core-js's Snapshot.Reader (every source file checked against its attachment's size and hash), and writes nothing unless every file reads — then writes the resources as Snapshot.WriteOrder's batch bundles, in reference order, through the route context's authed runner, and shows every entry's outcome grouped by response status.",
